let me show you one of my favor@@ ites .
suppose you like to square numbers , and frank@@ ly , who doesn &apos;t ?
let &apos;s look at the squ@@ ar@@ es of the first few fi@@ bon@@ acc@@ i numbers .
so one squ@@ ared is one , two squ@@ ared is four , three squ@@ ared is nine , five squ@@ ared is 25 , and so on .
but you wouldn &apos;t expect anything special to happen when you add the squ@@ ar@@ es together .
