and speaking of values , i &apos;ve noticed that in the discussion about moral per@@ su@@ asi@@ on online , and when i &apos;m talking with people , more often than not there is a weird bi@@ as .
and that bi@@ as is that we &apos;re asking , is this or that &quot; still &quot; eth@@ ical ?
is it &quot; still &quot; per@@ mis@@ si@@ ble ?
we &apos;re asking things like , is this ox@@ fa@@ m don@@ ation form -- where the regular mon@@ th@@ ly don@@ ation is the pres@@ et de@@ fau@@ lt and people , maybe without inten@@ ding it , are that way encoura@@ ged or nu@@ d@@ ged into giving a regular don@@ ation instead of a one-@@ time don@@ ation -- is that still per@@ mis@@ si@@ ble ?
