so the old days before digital radio when you were tun@@ ing in your radio and you heard &quot; cr@@ r@@ c@@ ck@@ k@@ k &quot; on the station you wanted to hear , that was the noise .
but more generally , this noise is something that cor@@ rup@@ ts the signal .
so for example , if you put your hand under a table and try to lo@@ c@@ alize it with your other hand , you can be off by several centi@@ meters due to the noise in sensor@@ y feedback .
