this is the challenge .
the reason this is happening bo@@ ils down , in my mind , to one basic problem , which is our in@@ ability to percei@@ ve the difference between public benefits and private prof@@ its .
we tend to constantly ignor@@ e public wealth simply because it is in the common wealth , it &apos;s common goods .
and here &apos;s an example from th@@ a@@ il@@ and where we found that , because the value of a man@@ gro@@ ve is not that much -- it &apos;s about $ 600 over the life of nine years that this has been measu@@ red -- compared to its value as a sh@@ ri@@ mp farm , which is more like $ 9@@ ,@@ 600 , there has been a gradu@@ al trend to de@@ ple@@ te the man@@ gro@@ ves and conver@@ t them to sh@@ ri@@ mp far@@ ms .
but of course , if you look at exactly what those prof@@ its are , almost 8@@ ,000 of those dollars are , in fact , sub@@ si@@ dies .
